[Music]  i guess there's a certain part of me  that's always thought that computer  parts look like cities  my name is zaid mink i'm an 18 year old  artist from zimbabwe  i grew up in a family of  nine people  my parents had a repurposing attitude  towards most things how can we use the  rubbish to make something else  so i just make  my artwork out of the things that i find  and the things that i collect  [Music]  i grew up in harare the capital city of  zimbabwe and i really like it there  but we do have quite a few challenges  like political unrest and economic  challenges  there's also e-waste dumping that has  affected many of the poorer areas around  the city  [Music]  this project that i'm working on is a  collaboration with hpe to make an area  of westminster done in recycled  electronics  i think what i'm doing on a small scale  is basically what they doing on a large  scale in a slightly different way  the parts for this project were from  hpe's facility  it was quite different compared to what  happened for my first project  with that one i had to go around asking  friends and family and trying to  scavenge things from side of the road  when planning for this project i used a  lot of online resources to calculate  what area i want to do  it was also quite helpful to see things  in person it puts things in perspective  quite nicely  from there i sketch out the layout of  the city and i just start building the  individual buildings one by one  i think in a perfect tool there wouldn't  be  such a thing as waste everything would  be  reused and repurposed for something else  there are about 50 million tons of  e-waste generated on an annual basis and  substances that go into the products  have impacts to soil water human health  we can't just take make dispose anymore  we need to really think about how we  responsibly design manufacture and  dispose of the products or potentially  reuse them at their end of life  the circular economy is a shift from the  traditional linear economy into a model  where it's regenerative in nature  one of the most exciting aspects of our  environmental program are our technology  renewal centers  of the material that comes in the door  over 89 is actually refurbished  remarketed and sold to new customers the  remaining portion is recycled in a  responsible way to have real impact at  scale  in the future if companies embrace the  idea of the circular economy e-waste  might not be an issue  and my artwork might be seen as a sort  of  weird historical artifact from a time  when we didn't know any better  [Music]  you

